1. f4 Nf6 2. Nf3 { Normally white wants to control the white squares for his strong white bishop. Now however white chooses to control the black ones so putting the dark bishop on b2 is desirable. } { [%csl Ge5,Gd4] } 2... d5 { Black now wants to control teh white squares. This tension will be the main concern throughout the game. } 3. e3 { This opens the diagonal for the white bishop. Allowing an attack with c4 on the d5 pawn. At the samen time the two pawns on g2 and h2 are still safe enough for the white King to hide under. } { [%csl Ge5,Gd4,Gc3,Gc4,Gg5,Gh4,Gd3,Gb5,Ga6,Ge2] } 3... c5 4. Be2 Nc6 5. O-O { Quick castling is important because the f2 square is a weakness. } 5... e6 6. b3 Bd6 7. Bb2 { E3 is a weakness so do not move the d2 pawn! } 7... d4 8. c3 dxe3 9. dxe3 *


